" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x=3+y \\\\ 5y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $10$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+5y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "810204698a78ba1cb5afaa72b36bf511cb2fa072080f2ad972c8d6a4ce865887" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{30}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f5fd037cacc3087bdce6c46f08df39056432b1e05f9b87e69a40066cef54a9d" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4508.json" "file_sha256" "8dbf2336da80cfbac224d2e80271fc7b3c87ddf08d14af4eef26e54b0cc12421" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4508.json" "file_sha256" "8dbf2336da80cfbac224d2e80271fc7b3c87ddf08d14af4eef26e54b0cc12421" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4509.json" "file_sha256" "c3928bc449a629e04a71b31cd9da9f639f723ca981c395ce7ef133c12a992ec3" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4509.json" "file_sha256" "c3928bc449a629e04a71b31cd9da9f639f723ca981c395ce7ef133c12a992ec3" "basis" 1063 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=7 \\\\ 5x+2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c72c700c448c2af12a1a7eec055362ede062cfde4e360a91101c1cb9ad6dc5e" "basis" 1087 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c72c700c448c2af12a1a7eec055362ede062cfde4e360a91101c1cb9ad6dc5e" "basis" 1087 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/e