n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "51e383b66a7c493103bd9ecd9597903735afe3c69fed707acfd713ea45ede6c8" "basis" 1180 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "51e383b66a7c493103bd9ecd9597903735afe3c69fed707acfd713ea45ede6c8" "basis" 1180 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/activity-met