ield/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-320792" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-32138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-y=17 \\\\ x+4y=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-32138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-32138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-32138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-32138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-32138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 2x+2y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x+2y=-1 \\\\ x-3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275758" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x=3+y \\\\ 5y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $10$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+5y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{30}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-321439" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5=2x-3y \\\\ 4x=y-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y=x+3 \\\\ 7-y=-x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y=3 \\\\ x-y=-7.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-102807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=1-3y \\\\ 3-4y=2x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+3y=1 \\\\ -2x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y=1-3x \\\\ x-2=-4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y=1 \\\\ x+4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4442bb9731647fee12b9445170a96f69aef8430d929cfae382f6c161545bf4c1"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "q-275763" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9528ae20a9568dd6f5c49ebe5bdefdef1ab3c42176fdab6cd2f5012305c6d7c"} {"question" "e-4508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/example-4508.json" "file_sha256" "2eb0a96e5cb3f1537a341a3cd88922cd8800d32553e812b182b5cc67785ea4e2"} {"question" "e-4508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/example-4508.json" "file_sha256" "2eb0a96e5cb3f1537a341a3cd88922cd8800d32553e812b182b5cc67785ea4e2"} {"question" "e-4509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/example-4509.json" "file_sha256" "2473c6be9cd14cb77d27610c40f46cfb3e09c2032246f44cab7c853fb74245f3"} {"question" "e-4509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/example-4509.json" "file_sha256" "2473c6be9cd14cb77d27610c40f46cfb3e09c2032246f44cab7c853fb74245f3"} {"question" "q-31893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "d6cca11344d5f90f02aa8e9974a269eb8724ec3a708c5ba7de03476bf22f1771" "reviewer_session" "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca" "rationale" "The coefficient matrix A=[[1,-2],[2,2]] has determinant 6, so A inverse is (1/6)[[2,2],[-2,1]]. Multiplying by [1,-1] gives the solution vector [0,-1/2], which satisfies both equations. Original option 2 and the stored answer express this same product, in the same multiplication order. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the original system and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns the submitted negative coefficient, not this reviewed answer." "bindings" {"problem" "282a75954b265c8757170d98fcd185535579c378b1c12cf9da882537522d1d55" "worked_solution" "49d6b639720924c8af1a1e3b0b918d1ae5725ef6670c437edc8151963c7de83f" "original_field" "14a107019e182abadbc769e5299a50ff03ff18710d4ee1cca9faaf6e2cc598f1" "reviewed_field" "0d9e0cab365d7db18f93a3b90a367f38218a20a18ba3252bb262bba3fa9435ba" "raw_widget" "0c8a4809998a8e3c35293223b270e8610a22d26b816f1d6c06c17d11009abbff"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-31893-before.png" "sha256" "d526e6af74d3ead68a69d5c23973535f4ba63267c834bf81e1427a2396164f3b"} {"path" "history-q-31893.png" "sha256" "68ca0db233a93d110c834eae1690e7fece7ca848e525ecf9c9f817762fd905e5"} {"path" "q-31893-after.json" "sha256" "dd103277c4915978b48823c3e0bd30b695f806a09ea03e5f4419d19ca52ad004"}]} {"question" "q-31893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "d6cca11344d5f90f02aa8e9974a269eb8724ec3a708c5ba7de03476bf22f1771" "rationale" "The coefficient matrix A=[[1,-2],[2,2]] has determinant 6, so A inverse is (1/6)[[2,2],[-2,1]]. Multiplying by [1,-1] gives the solution vector [0,-1/2], which satisfies both equations. Original option 2 and the stored answer express this same product, in the same multiplication order. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the original system and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns the submitted negative coefficient, not this reviewed answer."}] "usage" {"q-320805" [] "e-4508" [] "q-321439" [] "q-102806" [] "e-4509" [] "q-102809" [] "q-31893" []} "basis" 1768 "retractions" [[17592186092625 :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n${x - 2y = 1; 2x + 2y =-1$"] [17592186092625 :question/answer-fields 17592186090231] [17592186091970 :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"] [17592186091971 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186090232 17592186090233 17592186090234 17592186090235 17592186090236 17592186284736 17592186284737 17592186284738 17592186284739 17592186284740 17592186284786 17592186284788 17592186284790 17592186286343 17592186286344 17592186286346 17592186286348 17592186291758 17592186291759 17592186291760 17592186291761 17592186291762] "immutable_fields" [[17592186090231 :answer-field/correct] [17592186090231 :answer-field/id] [17592186090231 :answer-field/key] [17592186090231 :answer-fiel